# ~/.config/charter/env for charter-host (mode 600). Every variable: docs/env.md.
# install-host.sh copies this file into place when there is none, with USER and HOST_NAME filled in.
# No secrets here: CHARTER_CLAIM_KEY_FILE names the file that holds one.

# This host's public https:// address. Caddy terminates TLS for it and proxies to CHARTER_HOST_PORT on
# loopback. Its normalized form is the host's identity at the door (hostId = sha256 of it).
CHARTER_HOST_URL=https://HOST_NAME
# The Base address the door's vouchers pay; the facilitator settles your claims to it.
CHARTER_HOST_PAY_TO=0x0000000000000000000000000000000000000000
# The x402 claim key: one 0x + 64 hex private key, mode 400. It signs claims and refunds on the door's
# channel and holds no funds. Make it once: node deploy/door/new-claim-key.mjs /home/USER/.config/charter/claim-key
CHARTER_CLAIM_KEY_FILE=/home/USER/.config/charter/claim-key
# The door this host registers with (POST /v1/hosts) and answers. The default:
CHARTER_DOOR_URL=https://charterhome.dev
# The loopback port charter-host listens on, the one Caddy proxies to.
CHARTER_HOST_PORT=7401
# Who settles the door's vouchers. Default PayAI, which needs no key.
# X402_FACILITATOR_URL=https://facilitator.payai.network

CHARTER_DATA_DIR=/home/USER/.local/share/charter
# charter-job-python is required: the door's probe is a python job. Add charter-home and charter-hermes
# once homes are set up (install-home.sh, CHARTER_MAX_HOMES).
CHARTER_ALLOW_IMAGES=charter-job-python,charter-job-fetch
CHARTER_OFFER_ID=main
# One paid interval and its price, in micro-USDC: one hour at 0.007 USDC is about 5 USDC for 30 days.
# The door's probe pays at most 10000 (0.01 USDC) a tick: a host priced above that is never listed.
# Opens and status reads are free; only ticks are paid.
CHARTER_INTERVAL_SECONDS=3600
CHARTER_TICK_PRICE=7000
# gVisor for every job (install-host.sh installs and registers runsc). Recommended: renters run their
# own code here.
CHARTER_RUNTIME=runsc
# Live leases at once. Each takes 1 CPU and 1 GiB while it runs. A restart of the host program leaves
# running containers alone; only a lease whose container is not running is closed, and such a home is
# re-created while its paid time lasts. A lease only created, not started, is closed: check first
# (docs/ops.md).
CHARTER_MAX_LEASES=1
# Job egress through a SOCKS proxy (set: the offer says hiddenEgress), and the hidden-host badge.
# CHARTER_PROXY=socks5://172.17.0.1:9150
# CHARTER_HIDDEN_HOST=true
# Optional: your X handle. Your offer then states it, and Charter's X account names you once that handle posts
# charter-host-<your hostId> at it. Unset: you are "a host".
# CHARTER_HOST_X_HANDLE=your_handle
# Where a proxied job's names resolve: Charter's anon on the docker bridge's gateway, once
# install-home.sh has run with JOB_DNS_ADDR=172.17.0.1. Unset: the host's own resolvers, so the
# names a renter fetches leave from the host's address.
# CHARTER_JOB_DNS=172.17.0.1

# Homes (charter-home, charter-hermes). Run deploy/host/install-home.sh first: it sets up the anon and
# the bridge these name. Homes live at once, counted inside CHARTER_MAX_LEASES. 0: no homes.
CHARTER_MAX_HOMES=0
# A public dotted IPv4 address homes are reached on (no scheme, no port; a hostname is refused, since
# docker binds this address). Set, the onion is off unless CHARTER_HOME_ONION=1, and the two anon
# variables below are not needed. Homes use ports 22000-22099.
# CHARTER_HOME_PUBLIC_HOST=
# CHARTER_HOME_ONION=1
# GiB of each new home's disk, 1 to 64 (default 2). The offer advertises it as home.diskGiB. Images are
# sparse: a new home is refused (`no disk`) unless the free space, less what every existing disk may
# still grow by, less this size, leaves 3 GiB. A disk that exists keeps the size it was made with.
# CHARTER_HOME_DISK_GIB=10
# Root homes: every home made from now on is reached as root as well as tenant, apt works in it, and
# its /usr, /etc, /var, /root and /home/tenant live on its own disk. Refused unless
# CHARTER_RUNTIME=runsc. Homes that already exist keep the first layout. See docs/ops.md.
# CHARTER_HOME_ROOT=1
# With the onion on: Charter's anon includes this directory; the host writes one onion service per
# home here, and sends the pid in the pidfile SIGHUP after changing it.
# CHARTER_ANON_HS_DIR=/home/USER/.config/charter/anon/hs.d
# CHARTER_ANON_PIDFILE=/home/USER/.local/share/charter/anon/anon.pid
# Optional, shown at their defaults. The last three must match anonrc and charter-home-net.sh.
# Per home: onion keys, disk image and the host's files for the box.
# CHARTER_HOME_DIR=/home/USER/.local/share/charter/homes
# The docker network charter-home-net.service makes, with its firewall.
# CHARTER_HOME_NETWORK=charter-home
# Its gateway, where anon listens; a home's DNS and proxies point here.
# CHARTER_HOME_GATEWAY=172.19.0.1
# Anon's SOCKS port (a home's ALL_PROXY).
# CHARTER_HOME_SOCKS_PORT=9050
# Anon's HTTP tunnel port (a home's HTTP_PROXY and HTTPS_PROXY).
# CHARTER_HOME_HTTP_PORT=9080
